      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-15384",
      ":question/problem": "A thermometer is placed into a water bath and displays a reading of ${50}^{\u2218}C.$ The thermometer is then transferred to a ${10}^{\u2218}C$ water bath, and its reading begins to decrease. After $5$ minutes, the thermometer reading is ${40}^{\u2218}C.$ To the nearest minute, how long does it take for the thermometer to register a reading of ${30}^{\u2218}C?$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that the temperature reading $T(t)$ of the thermometer decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling, where $T$ is measured in degrees Celsius and $t>0$ is the time, in minutes, since the thermometer was transferred into the ${10}^{\u2218}C$ water bath.*"
